    <canvas id="webgl-bg-canvas" data-terrain-theme="light" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <section class="platform-hero" id="terranean-hero">
        <div class="platform-hero-content">
            <span class="tag">Terranean Etiology</span>
            <h1>Causal Forensics<br>at the Scale of Reality</h1>
            <p>Continuously reconstruct the full causal graph of the environment — the chains of decisions, logistics movements, influence operations, and human relationships that produced the present moment.</p>
            <a href="#overview" class="cta-link-arrow" style="margin-top: 40px; color: var(--text-light);">Explore Etiology <span>↓</span></a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <main class="main-content">

        <div class="prose-section" id="overview">
            <h2>The Discipline of Origin</h2>
            <p>Etiology is the discipline of origin. It continuously reconstructs the full causal graph of the environment: the chains of decisions, logistics movements, influence operations, equipment states, human relationships, and environmental factors that produced the present moment.</p>
            <p>Every significant event is treated as a node with ancestry. Every anomaly is traced through multi-hop causal paths. Alternative histories are generated and ranked. Confidence is quantified. Gaps in the graph are surfaced rather than ignored.</p>
            <p>The result is digital forensics elevated from after-action review into continuous, real-time operational capability. Commanders and analysts no longer ask only "what occurred?" They ask, and receive structured answers to, <strong>"what sequence of causes made this inevitable, what interventions would have altered the path, and what latent causal structures remain active beneath the surface?"</strong></p>
            <p>Etiology turns the past from a static record into a living diagnostic instrument.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Core Capabilities</h2>
            <div class="architecture-grid">
                <div class="architecture-card">
                    <span class="card-tag">/01 Causal Graph Construction</span>
                    <h3>Continuous Reconstruction</h3>
                    <p>Continuous or on-demand causal graph construction from heterogeneous data sources — events, logs, sensor feeds, human reports, and external intelligence — maintaining a living model of the operational environment.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="architecture-card">
                    <span class="card-tag">/02 Path Discovery</span>
                    <h3>Multi-Hop Causal Tracing</h3>
                    <p>Multi-hop causal path discovery with confidence scoring and alternative-history ranking. Every anomaly is traced through its ancestry, surfacing the chains that produced the present moment.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="architecture-card">
                    <span class="card-tag">/03 Gap Detection</span>
                    <h3>Surfacing the Unknown</h3>
                    <p>Surfaces missing CausalNodes or low-confidence edges that require additional collection or human adjudication. Gaps in the graph are treated as operational signals, not oversights.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="architecture-card">
                    <span class="card-tag">/04 Counterfactual Analysis</span>
                    <h3>Alternative Histories</h3>
                    <p>Given a CausalGraph, evaluate the effect of intervening on specific nodes and edges. Generate and rank alternative histories to understand what interventions would have altered the path.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="editorial-callout">
            <h2 class="editorial-callout-text">
                Etiology turns the past from a static record into a living diagnostic instrument. The past is no longer opaque.
            </h2>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>How Etiology Works</h2>
            <div class="workflow-steps">
                <div class="workflow-step">
                    <span class="step-num">/01</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Ingest & Reconstruct</h3>
                        <p>Heterogeneous data sources are continuously ingested. Events, decisions, logistics movements, and observations are mapped into CausalNodes within the operational graph.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-media">
                        <img src="../panteon-software.png" alt="Causal reconstruction interface">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="workflow-step">
                    <span class="step-num">/02</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Trace & Score</h3>
                        <p>Multi-hop causal paths are discovered and scored for confidence. Alternative histories are generated and ranked. Gaps in the causal graph are surfaced for further investigation.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-media">
                        <img src="../panteon-software.png" alt="Causal path tracing interface">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="workflow-step">
                    <span class="step-num">/03</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Analyze & Act</h3>
                        <p>Counterfactual analysis evaluates interventions. Forensic replay reconstructs the state of the graph at any prior timestamp. Results feed into Teleology for forward-looking purpose modeling.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-media">
                        <img src="../panteon-software.png" alt="Counterfactual analysis interface">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" style="text-align: center; padding-bottom: 140px;">
            <h2>Explore Terranean</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 520px; margin: 0 auto 40px; font-size: 1rem;">Etiology for the roots. Teleology for the ends. See how both systems work together in the developer documentation.</p>
            <a href="../developers/terranean-documentation.html" class="get-started-btn" style="display:inline-flex;background-color:var(--text-dark);color:var(--text-light);border-color:var(--text-dark);padding:14px 40px;font-size:0.85rem;text-decoration:none">Read Documentation</a>
        </section>

    </main>

